		{
			"id": "114914145503870838",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@fvsch/114914145456493090",
			"author": {
				"name": "Florens Verschelde",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@fvsch",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/834/091/035/043/627/original/4367bd08dd68da57.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-07-25T13:38:25.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> &gt; As an aside, this search has made me tempted to ask: do we need to keep Dual publishing packages? I prefer ESM over CJS but maybe just pick one?</p><p>Some in the ecosystem think that we don't need to anymore, and should just ship ESM modules (see for instance <a href=\"https://e18e.dev/blog/migrating-the-ecosystem-to-esm.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">e18e.dev/blog/migrating-the-ec</span><span class=\"invisible\">osystem-to-esm.html</span></a>), but it depends on what older Node.js versions you want to support.</p><p>- Supported and updated versions of Node 20 and 22? You can ship ESM only.<br>- Node 18 or earlier? Early (and at this point not secure) versions of Node 20 and 22? Then you need a dual package.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114914171820840463",
			"parentId": "114914145503870838",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/114914171820840463",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-07-25T13:45:08.108Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@fvsch\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>fvsch</span></a></span> for the record I have never dual published a package. When 11ty swapped to ESM we went all-in on ESM with Node 18+ and it has worked fine.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
